    {
      "text": "axe is laid unto the root of the trees, Matt. 3:10 (Luke 3:9; Alma 5:52; D&C 97:7). because they had no root, they withered, Matt. 13:6 (Mark 4:6; Luke 8:13). tares, ye root up also the wheat with them, Matt. 13:29. plant, which my heavenly Father hath not planted, shall be rooted up, Matt. 15:13. if the root be holy, so are the branches, Rom. 11:16. being rooted and grounded in love, Eph. 3:17. Rooted and built up in him, Col. 2:7. love of money is the root of all evil, 1 Tim. 6:10. trees … plucked up by the roots, Jude 1:12. Lion of the tribe of Juda, the Root of David, Rev. 5:5. I am the root and the offspring of David, Rev. 22:16.",
